-- Sovietski: the Rusalka and Thunderfist Superheavy Machines, WB36 cyborg bodies with no WB17 counterpart, held as new rows (printed 139-145).
-- 2 vehicle rows, with 21 locations and 9 weapon entries.
--
-- One-off data script, run once per environment. NOT a migration - it adds
-- rows, not schema.
--
--   node scripts/d1-apply.mjs --local apps/character-creator/db/~396-sovietski-cyborgs-c.sql
--
-- Written by scripts/vessel-sql.mjs from 1 worker file(s). Every value
-- is printable ASCII, every row cites its book, and a Main Body location
-- agrees with its vehicle's mdc_main_body.

INSERT OR IGNORE INTO vehicles (slug, name, system, vehicle_class, crew, passengers, speed_ground, speed_air, speed_water, dimensions, weight_tons, mdc_main_body, is_mega_damage, ar, cost, cost_note, description, source_book) VALUES
  ('sovietski-rusalka-superheavy-machine', 'Sovietski Rusalka Superheavy Machine', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One human volunteer (full conversion).', 'None.', 'Running: 90 mph (144 km) maximum, with or without its cyborg armor. Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or 25 feet (7.6 m) lengthwise, +50% with a running start. Jet Nodes cannot be fitted.', 'None. The underwater propulsion system takes the place of flight.', 'Swims 15 mph (24 km) without its thrusters. With them: 35 mph (56 km; 30 knots) submerged and 45 mph (72 km; 39 knots) on the surface. Can also walk the bottom of rivers, lakes and shallow seas at 8 mph (13 km). Four hours of oxygen; maximum depth 3,000 feet (914 m).', 'Height 10 feet (3 m); width 3 feet, 8 inches (1.1 m); length 3 feet (0.9 m).', 'One ton.', 260, 1, NULL, 3400000, 'Sovietski cost 3.4 million credits; 5.9 million credits on the Black Market, rare. The Sovietski figure is stored.', 'The Sovietski''s naval assault cyborg, the first of its Superheavy Machines (the class that now holds the old Shocktrooper designs such as the Thunderhammer, Thunderstrike and Thunderstorm). Named for the water demon of Russian folklore, it was built to fight the piracy of Horune, Brodkil and Warlord raiders on Russia''s lakes and rivers, and for naval work generally: striking enemy craft, scouting ahead of beach landings, and knocking out guard posts, turrets, sensors and communications before an assault comes ashore. Clumsy and unable to Prowl on land, it is stealthy in the water, and below about 25 knots sonar tends to read it as a walrus or a giant squid. Groups of two to four close on a ship submerged, then mine the hull, or climb aboard by harpoon and tentacle; on deck they swing from masts, rails and turrets on their four tentacles, pick off officers and sensors, and hurl sailors over the side. Twenty to forty of them with light marine support can take most small and medium pirate ships, Horune included, while leaving the vessel and its plunder intact, though hostages are better left to Spetsnaz Commandos, since the Rusalka is too heavy-handed for a rescue. It also does salvage, simple hull repairs, search and rescue, and towing of small craft. A ballast system keeps it afloat; two main thrusters on the back and many small ones over the body drive it in and under the water. Robot P.S. 35 and Robot P.P. 22: 1D4 M.D. restrained punch, 2D4 M.D. full punch, 4D4 M.D. power punch, 2D4 M.D. kick, 2D8 M.D. leap kick (power punch and leap kick each use two attacks). Bonuses: three extra attacks per melee for the four tentacles, +20% to Climbing, initiative +1, strike, parry and dodge +4, entangle +2, pull punch +2. Penalties: -40% to Prowl, and with tactile sensitivity of 40%, -40% to Forgery, Picking Locks, Picking Pockets, surgery, Whittling/Sculpting, Art and any fine-fingered skill. Nuclear, 20-year average life. Bionic features: every standard Sovietski Heavy Machine feature, plus a targeting sight eye, an enhanced oxygen storage cell (four hours), a depth gauge and alarm, and gills. Starting weapons and features: one weapon and one feature of choice per hand, two more bionic weapons, tools or features in the left forearm only (the harpoon launcher and winch fill the right), a face (usually a younger version of its own, hidden by the helmet), handheld weapons sized for a Heavy or Superheavy Machine (energy weapons are preferred for boardings and beach assaults), and two Micro-Repair Robots plus two Cyber-Nano-Robot Repair Systems. It may take no leg compartments or concealed leg weapon rods, which would weaken the legs at depth. Heavy Rusalka armor and helmet add 240 M.D.C. to the main body and 80 to the head. Chop-shops, Warlord camps, Mindwerks and some mercenaries will fit its weapon systems to Shocktroopers or Superheavy Machines for a price.', 'Rifts World Book 36: Sovietski p.139-142'),
  ('sovietski-thunderfist-superheavy-machine', 'Sovietski Thunderfist Superheavy Machine', 'rifts', 'borg', 'One human volunteer (full conversion).', 'None.', 'Running: 50 mph (80 km) maximum. Leaping: 15 feet (4.6 m) high or 20 feet (6.1 m) lengthwise, +30% with a running start.', 'None; too heavy and bulky to fly.', 'Cannot swim and sinks. With an oxygen storage cell it walks the bottom of rivers and waterways at 8 mph (13 km). Maximum depth 1,200 feet (366 m).', 'Height 13 feet (4 m), 8 feet (2.4 m) hunched over; width 5 feet, 6 inches (1.7 m); length 4 feet (1.2 m).', '4 tons.', 580, 1, NULL, 5500000, 'Sovietski cost 5.5 million credits; 8-9 million credits on the Black Market, rare. The Sovietski figure is stored.', 'The newest of the Sovietski''s Superheavy Machines, an experimental four-armed brawler answering the Warlords'' Heavy Shocktroopers and built from the strongest bionics its Cyber-Docs have yet made. Its job is close combat against Brodkil, Gargoyles, Warlord Shocktroopers and foreign robots and power armor: its armored fists smash vehicles and tear apart Light Machines and foot soldiers, and every fist carries triple-barreled Bulletdusters that go off as a punch lands, a crack of gunfire on each blow that gave the cyborg its name. Like the Thunderstorm it often moves and rests stooped like a gorilla, weighed down by its built-in plating and outsized upper arms. That armor lets it soak heavy fire as it closes, and built-in nano-repair systems patch armor and weapons during long missions. An ion blaster in each right forearm, a chainsaw in each left forearm and a grenade launcher over the right shoulder (described as rapid-fire in the text, single shots only in the weapon entry) keep massed infantry from swarming it. Robot P.S. 40 and Robot P.P. 22: 1D4 M.D. restrained punch, 2D6 M.D. full punch, 4D6 M.D. power punch, 3D8 M.D. kick, 5D8 M.D. leap kick (power punch and leap kick each use two attacks); a full speed ram or body block does 3D6 M.D., uses two attacks, and has a 01-50% chance to knock down anyone under a ton, who loses one attack and initiative. Bonuses: two extra attacks per melee for the four arms, one more at levels 5 and 10, +20% to Climbing, initiative +2, strike and parry +5, dodge +3, entangle +2, pull punch +2, roll with impact +2. Penalties: -50% to Prowl, and with tactile sensitivity of 35%, -40% to Forgery, Picking Locks, Picking Pockets, surgery, Whittling/Sculpting, Art and any fine-fingered skill. Its stat block prints no power system; its blasters run off a nuclear supply. Bionic features: every standard Sovietski Heavy Machine feature, plus a combat computer, wide-angle vision and a multi-optic eye, one secret chest compartment, the second pair of arms, and a climb cord in the wrists of any two arms. Starting weapons and features: one leg compartment or leg weapon per leg, a face (usually a younger version of its own, hidden by the helmet in combat), three more eye or head features, handheld weapons sized for a Heavy or Superheavy Machine only, and three Micro-Repair Robots plus two Cyber-Nano-Robot Repair Systems. Its armor is built into the body, so it takes no add-on plating; only the helmet adds 80 M.D.C. to the head. Chop-shops, Warlord camps, Mindwerks and some mercenaries will fit its weapon systems to Shocktroopers or Superheavy Machines for a price.', 'Rifts World Book 36: Sovietski p.142-145');

